==Portuguese==
{{wikipedia|lang=pt}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|roa-opt|pt}} {{term|poder|lang=roa-opt}}, from {{etyl|VL.|pt}} *''potēre'', from {{etyl|la|pt}} {{term|posse|lang=la}}, present active infinitive of {{term|possum|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|PT}} {{IPA|/pu.ˈðeɾ/|lang=pt}}
* {{a|Paulista}} {{IPA|/po.ˈde(ɹ)/|lang=pt}}

===Noun===
{{pt-noun|m|es}}

# [[power]]

===Verb===
{{pt-verb||poder}}

# [[can]] (to be able)
#: '''''Posso''' ir na sua casa?'' {{qualifier|Brazil}}
#: '''''Posso''' ir a sua casa?'' {{qualifier|Portugal}}
#:: '''Can''' I go to your house.?

====Usage notes====
This verb is replaced with ''[[saber]]'' for use with skills (as in to know how to do something) and omitted when relating to verbs of sense.
* "You are allowed to do it." - "Podes fazê-lo" (with poder)
* "She can (is allowed to) swim." (as said by the Doctor after an operation) - "Ela pode nadar" (with poder)
* "She can (knows how to) swim." (not in medical kind of context) - "Ela sabe nadar" (with saber)
* "I am able to see it." - "Eu vejo-o" (omitted)

====Conjugation====
{{pt-conj||poder}}

